 "D366": {"key": "paper", "value": {"season": [0, 0.22, 0.45, 0.68, 0.85, 1], "step": 2, "year": 7919, "light": {"slope": 0.6, "patch": 0.07, "sun": 0.22, "shade": 0.3}, "shadow": {"dx": 0.8, "dy": 1.2, "w": 1.6}, "snow": {"steps": 6}, "marsh": {"tussock": 0.2}, "reeds": {"n": 6, "w": 0.6, "lean": 2, "tall": [3, 3]}, "glint": {"per": 0.08, "len": [2, 5], "w": 1, "rate": 1.2, "a": 0.6, "near": 1.5}, "water": [1.5, 4], "blades": [1.1, 1.767], "level": 4, "mini": 0.25, "blade": {"tiles": [[103.6, 297], [64, 113], [39.6, 45]], "len": [1.6, 2.2], "lean": 1.8, "w": 0.34, "tall": 1.3, "least": 8, "seed": 13}, "cloud": {"tile": 256, "cell": 64, "per": 4, "oct": 4, "k": 3.2, "a": 0.243, "scale": 13.2, "drift": [22, 9], "seed": 5, "byte": 255, "ms": 1000}}, "name": "the paper ground (N11, Albert Nov 10): season is where in the year (0 to 1) each season colour is full; step rounds the colour so the grass is coloured again only when it moves a visible step; year is a prime that gives each year's flowers new places; light: the hills' sun and shade (slope) and the meadow's soft patches (patch), at most sun and shade; shadow: the thin shadow each sheet casts on the one below; snow: six steps, hollows first; marsh: shallow water laid as one smooth sheet with the shallows, after the grass's colour, a share tussock of its tiles left standing as grass tussocks (Albert, Nov 10, #9: tussock sedge marsh); reeds in the marsh's water; glints on the water: one in per tiles, length, width, how fast they come and go, how bright, from what zoom; water: how far from its shore (in tiles) the water turns mid and then deep, as a lake deepens away from its bank; blade tiles: the second at the first over the golden ratio (64 / 1.618 = 39.6), the number least near any fraction (Hurwitz), so the two never line up in a repeat the eye can see, its blade count scaled by area to keep the density (Albert, Nov 10, #1); a third tile one golden step up (64 × 1.618 = 103.6) and every count two thirds, so no one tile carries enough of the blades for its own repeat to show close in, at the same density (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #17: the pattern still showed at close zoom); blades: the zoom where the blades start to show and where they are full (v80's: none from far away, full close up); N13, the paper ground mock built (Albert, Nov 10 08:38: 'Keep cloud shadows. And set water to high. Go go'): level: the water fills every cut up to this height (high; the wading depth), mini: the minimap picture's scale; blade: the mock's two tiles (size, count; the Cicada Principle), each blade a thin triangle len long, leaning lean, w wide, tall stretch, drawn at the screen's pixels for the zoom (never smaller than least); cloud: the mock's cloud shadows, a tile of soft noise (cell lattice, per waves across, oct octaves, contrast k, darkest a), laid scale ground units a pixel and drifting drift a second (the mock's, grown to this map's size)", "cite": ["N301", "N305", "N304"], "law": []},
